{
  "meta": {
    "title": "Bug Hunt Bench",
    "subtitle": "105 real bugs hidden in two production repos. Frontier coding models find and fix what they can, graded blind.",
    "planted_total": 105,
    "repo1_total": 45,
    "repo2_total": 60,
    "survivors": 49,
    "models": 17,
    "runs": 29,
    "updated": "2026-08-27",
    "source_repo": "https://github.com/phuryn/experiments/tree/main/bug-hunt-bench",
    "author": "Pawel Huryn",
    "author_url": "https://www.productcompass.pm",
    "author_x": "https://x.com/PawelHuryn"
  },
  "method": [
    "Two unrelated production codebases: a ~28K-line TypeScript VS Code extension (45 bugs) and a ~60K-line React/Supabase LMS (60 bugs). Most bugs are real regressions reverted from the repos' own fix history, each with its fix commit.",
    "The test suites stay green, so nothing points at the answers. Every model gets the identical prompt, one round per repo, in its own native agentic CLI.",
    "Grading is blind: the model's diff is the ground truth, not its report. An independent judge scores against a withheld answer key and never learns which model produced the diff.",
    "The score counts planted bugs only. Some models bug-max - they report a long list of real but irrelevant problems, and that list has no answer key and no ceiling, so counting it would just reward volume. Unplanted fixes are tracked separately and never scored."
  ],
  "glossary": {
    "fixed": "Planted bugs fixed and verified against the withheld answer key. The only number in the score.",
    "partial": "The defect was addressed but not fully closed. Not counted in the score.",
    "claimed_only": "Named in the model's report but not fixed in its diff - including bugs it saw and chose not to touch. Not counted in the score.",
    "extras": "A real defect the model fixed that nobody planted. Genuine work - but the set has no answer key and no ceiling, so it cannot be scored reliably. Counted, never added to the score.",
    "cost_bill": "An actual invoice or credits delta.",
    "cost_list": "A token-count estimate at published list rates, not a bill.",
    "cost_floor": "Reconstructed lower bound - this CLI reports context occupancy, not billing.",
    "cost_free": "Served free at the time of the run.",
    "effort_verified_ceiling": "This model's highest reasoning setting. We checked that changing the setting actually changes what the model does.",
    "effort_verified": "We checked that changing this reasoning setting actually changes what the model does.",
    "effort_first_party": "A setting the vendor documents in their own tool. Taken at face value, not separately tested.",
    "effort_clamped": "We asked for a higher setting and the tool quietly ran a lower one. Published as a correction.",
    "effort_inert_default": "This route ignores the effort setting entirely, so the model ran at its own default. There was no working dial to turn."
  },
  "caveats": [
    "One round per model per repo. Same-setting variance is real and measured: three Grok 4.5 runs on identical settings scored 16, 13 and 17.",
    "Wall clock is the same measure on every row: repo 1 plus repo 2 agent time, with dependency install and health checks excluded. Two things bend it, and both are marked on the score-and-time map. Three runs took their two repo legs concurrently - the sum is still like-for-like, but two agents sharing one machine and one API key contend, so those figures can run high rather than low. And one figure is adjusted: the retired-Gemini-CLI run excludes a 35-minute harness stall, the only number here that is not what the harness measured.",
    "Cost is not one kind of number: some figures are an actual bill, some are a token-count estimate at published list rates, one CLI only allows a reconstructed lower bound, and one run was free. The key under the board names which is which - they are not interchangeable, and none of them is a quote for what you would pay.",
    "49 of the 105 bugs have survived every model in every run to date. The count moves rarely - four bugs have ever come off it, two of them on 25 August 2026."
  ],
